1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,372
Every supplier bill and every bank
movement in Miftah needs

2
00:00:03,372 --> 00:00:06,407
two kinds of master data: vendors and bank
accounts.

3
00:00:06,407 --> 00:00:08,092
As the Accountant, open Vendors.

4
00:00:08,092 --> 00:00:11,127
Each supplier has its tax registration
number, a contact,

5
00:00:11,127 --> 00:00:14,162
and its own payable account in the ledger,
with

6
00:00:14,162 --> 00:00:16,859
what is open, overdue or paid in advance.

7
00:00:16,859 --> 00:00:18,545
Now add a new supplier.

8
00:00:18,545 --> 00:00:22,592
Select Add Vendor and enter the legal
name, Gulf Shield Pest Control.

9
00:00:22,592 --> 00:00:25,289
Enter the fifteen-digit TRN: without it,
the input

10
00:00:25,289 --> 00:00:27,987
VAT on this supplier's bills cannot be
claimed.

11
00:00:27,987 --> 00:00:31,358
Set the payment terms to 45 days, so every
bill

12
00:00:31,358 --> 00:00:34,393
gets its due date automatically, then the
contact details.

13
00:00:34,393 --> 00:00:37,091
You do not choose a payable account:
Miftah

14
00:00:37,091 --> 00:00:39,788
creates one for the vendor and keeps it.

15
00:00:39,788 --> 00:00:43,160
Save, and Gulf Shield appears with its own
payable account.

16
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:46,195
Open BlueWave Cleaning to see a vendor at
work.

17
00:00:46,195 --> 00:00:48,555
The header shows its TRN and terms.

18
00:00:48,555 --> 00:00:50,915
Open items lists every bill with its

19
00:00:50,915 --> 00:00:53,276
voucher, due date, amount, paid and open.

20
00:00:53,276 --> 00:00:56,985
The August bill, dated 25 August, falls
due on 24 September.

21
00:00:56,985 --> 00:00:59,345
The statement of account is a PDF

22
00:00:59,345 --> 00:01:01,705
for any dates, in English or Arabic.

23
00:01:01,705 --> 00:01:04,740
Bank accounts are set up by the Company
Admin.

24
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:08,449
Palm Ridge has two Emirates Islamic
accounts, one for each building.

25
00:01:08,449 --> 00:01:11,147
The account details stay hidden in this
video.

26
00:01:11,147 --> 00:01:15,193
Each bank account is linked to its
property and to that building's

27
00:01:15,193 --> 00:01:18,902
own bank account in the chart of accounts,
so a cleared

28
00:01:18,902 --> 00:01:22,611
cheque or a supplier payment lands in the
right building's books.

29
00:01:22,611 --> 00:01:24,297
One account is the default.

30
00:01:24,297 --> 00:01:27,669
Open one to edit it: the linked property,
the chart

31
00:01:27,669 --> 00:01:31,041
of accounts link, and the default flag are
all here.

32
00:01:31,041 --> 00:01:33,401
With vendors and bank accounts in place,

33
00:01:33,401 --> 00:01:35,424
every voucher has somewhere to post.
